00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.429 align:start position:0%
 
we've been spending the last month  putting a whole bunch of new 14 and  16-inch macbook pros through various  tests and comparisons and have also been  using my own personal 16-inch m1 max  model at my house basically every day  and unfortunately we've noticed quite a  few problems over this past month so in  this video i'm not only going to cover  those problems but i'm also going to  provide solutions for the ones that  actually have them or may have them soon  but don't get me wrong i absolutely love  my new 16 inch macbook pro for various  reasons and to be completely honest it's  the best apple device purchase i've made  in years but nevertheless there are some  problems that i want to be fully  transparent about because they are very  real and some of them have some  interesting fixes that you seriously  need to know about so let's get right  into problem number one one of the  things that was the most excited about  with these new macbook pros is the new  120hz promotion feature since i do a lot  of web browsing at home and i love how  smooth it is on my iphone 13 pro max but  to this day both safari and chrome are  still limited to 60 hertz scrolling  which is very unfortunate on these new  macbook pros now recently apple released  a new version of their safari technology  preview which claims that it supports  120 hertz scroll animations but everyone  on the internet says that it still  doesn't work so hopefully apple is going  to be working on a software fix soon  because they did intentionally show off  safari 120 hertz scrolling in their own  keynote video so they have to add it  soon now getting into the second problem  i recently upgraded my internet at my  house with centurylink fiber which now  supports speeds up to 940 gigabits per  second both up and down and while  testing the wired ethernet lan speeds  using a qnap gigabit ethernet adapter i  got very close to the full speeds which  was very impressive however when i  tested out the wi-fi it seemed to always  be slower than on my iphone 13 pro no  matter the location within my home up to  a difference of around 200 megabits per  second in certain spots which is a bit  disappointing since i need the faster  speeds on my macbook not on my iphone  and upon doing some research i found out  that the new macbook pros actually have  slightly slower wi-fi speeds compared to  older macbooks as you can see the  maximum phi data rate for ax wi-fi six  is actually a hundred megabits per  second slower than the ac wi-fi five  data rate on older max but making it  worse the wi-fi five speeds are  significantly slower at 866 megabits per  second compared to 1300 on older macs so  if you're still using a wi-fi 5 router  you'll likely see a downgrade in terms  of wi-fi speeds until you upgrade to a  new wi-fi 6 model moving on to the third  problem it's got to do with the new  notch now while i've personally gotten  used to it and i honestly don't mind the  look at all especially since it gives us  the super immersive display with thin  bezels there are a couple of issues that  you might experience thanks to the notch  first of all i've noticed that in some  games like rocket league that have  important ui elements in the top center  of the screen the notch can actually dig  in and cover important info at times and  other than that there are actually some  apps that have many menu bar items that  will be hidden underneath the notch like  quinn from snazzy labs showed us in a  recent tweet and finally if you have a  lot of menu bar items on the right side  like we do when we run our tests and  comparisons like for example to show cpu  temperature and fan speed some of them  will actually disappear if they get too  close to the notch which is very  annoying but in my daily use i haven't  really noticed it myself since i don't  really need to do any of that at home  but it is something that you could  potentially run into yourself for  problem number four i want to mention  that even after a year of the original  m1 max being out in the wild we still  have a lot of software and apps that  don't have full native apple silicon  support in terms of video editing using  final cut pro we've had to replace some  of our motion vfx plugins with ones that  may have missing features because they  just aren't supported anymore now of  course i know this is fully up to the  developers but it's already been a year  and a half since apple announced the  transition and this kind of stuff can  really slow down these new insanely fast  macbook pros for example the open source  blender rendering program still doesn't  support metal which makes rendering much  slower than it is on windows laptops  with traditional graphics cards that use  cuda or whatever else and then of course  there are issues with unsupported audio  plugins in logic pro so it sucks to see  that the transition still has a lot more  work before it's fully polished for  problem number five this is perhaps the  most annoying thing that i've  experienced at home and that's actually  display blooming as we all know the new  14 and 16 inch macbook pros come with  new mini led displays that can get  insanely bright while also having  incredibly dark levels of contrast  however since i don't personally have a  tv in my home i resort to using my  macbook pro to watch movies which is  great because of the new and improved  speakers but if the display isn't  pointed directly at you then the  blooming becomes noticeable and it's  actually quite distracting and the thing  i didn't expect was that i would notice  the blooming in shots that are more  dimly lit and hazy like many of the  shots from the movie dune and it just  gets so much worse when you're viewing  it from the side and especially if your  eyes are looking down at the display  which may happen when you're sitting  upright on your couch to maybe eat  snacks or grab a drink or whatever else  so with that said i actually have to be  intentional about how i place my macbook  pro when watching something to avoid  blooming which is a bit disappointing  but the display still looks so much  better than the previous ones so it's  still worth it for problem number six  we've been noticing that the viewing  angles in general aren't as good as they  were before causing the display to look  a bit dimmer from the side and the top  this is likely due to the switch to the  new mini led display tech since it has  more layers that are required to make it  look great with all of the local dimming  zones and everything else which also  makes it look a tad bit more cool toned  compared to before but once again when  you're looking straight at it there are  no issues at all and most people likely  won't even notice when looking from the  side for problem number seven we've been  suffering from that new memory leak  issue that has been messing with the  performance of the new macbook pros  especially when editing off of a nas  storage system causing a bunch of lag  and other issues so to quickly explain  this problem the ram that usually gets  cleared and swapped by your apps just  stops getting cleared and it keeps  filling up starving the rest of the  system and slowing down performance as  you can see in this clip which shows  windows server using up a massive 33  gigabytes of ram on my imac pro but  thankfully some users are reporting that  the latest beta version of macos  monterey has fixed this problem but of  course not everyone has access to the  beta or wants to upgrade to it so  hopefully the public release gets this  fixed soon now moving on to problem  number eight the 14 inch m1 max macbook  pro actually throttles the performance  quite a bit compared to the 16 inch  model which apple didn't mention  anything about in their keno for example  the gpu clock speed on the 14 inch will  not go higher than around 11 36  megahertz no matter what even if the  temperatures are cool and you're plugged  into power it's literally a hard cap by  apple since we weren't able to get more  than 35 watts of power flowing to the 14  inch m1 max's gpu compared to as high as  43 watts on the 16 inch model which can  get up to around the full  megahertz clock speed which is around 14  higher than on the 14 inch which of  course leads to faster performance  across the board as you can see in the  gfx bench graphics test and based on all  of the other tests that we ran the  biggest performance difference we saw  was when we tested cinebench and 3dmark  wildlife at the same time and the  16-inch ended up being 37 faster which  is a huge jump but don't get me wrong  the 14 inch is still more than powerful  enough for almost everyone and is by far  the fastest laptop in its size and  weight class which is why max recently  returned his 16-inch and stuck to the  14-inch for the awesome portability so  definitely check out his video on that  if you haven't already for problem  number nine this finally brings us into  gaming support i've already created two  gaming reviews using both the m1 pro and  m1 max macbook pros and they gave us  very impressive performance at least for  the games that actually worked games  with mac os ports ran very well like  diablo 3 starcraft 2 dota 2 and  minecraft but some games just didn't  perform that well like cs go but the  worst part is that bootcamp support is  now gone so you have to resort to using  apps like parallel 17 and crossover 21  to play windows games and while they in  fact do an excellent job there is still  so much translation going on that it  greatly slows down their performance  compared to playing native games for  example we had to turn the settings way  down to get grand theft auto 5 to run at  60fps on the m1 max macbook pro which  keep in mind is a very expensive machine  but playing world of warcraft which is  native was amazing easily getting over  with the settings turned way up and  matthew moniz even showed that it was  almost as fast as a 3080 mobile gpu  laptop which i don't think anybody was  expecting but the issue is that there  are barely any native games and even  with crossover 21 direct x12 windows  games aren't supported yet so you're  pretty much limited to older aaa game  titles but the worst part of all is that  games that use kernel-based anti-cheat  won't run at all so you simply can't  play any online games like call of duty  vanguard and we're not even sure how  long it's gonna take before they finally  can but thankfully there is a chance we  could get boot camp support in the  future since qualcomm had a secret  exclusivity deal with windows on arm  which might be why boot camp support  disappeared and since we know nvidia is  working on an arm-based gaming laptop we  should hopefully get anti-cheat support  for armed ships in the future and  finally for problem number 10 while the  microphone quality has definitely  improved compared to older macbooks it  sometimes sounds a bit dull or muted  when you have some background noise in  the room so it almost seems like it's  over compensating for the noise  therefore cutting out the high end of  the vocal range compared to older  macbooks so just hear it for yourself  and now let's compare the webcams i have  both opened up right here and i'm gonna  switch between them as far as the video  and the audio so you guys can compare  which one looks better and which one  sounds better now there is a chance that  this is a bug that can be fixed in the  future but it's definitely a bit odd to  hear right now but don't worry this is a  very minimal issue and it's unlikely to  bother a lot of people since the quality  is already so much better than basically  any other windows laptop microphone  system out there so with all that said  those are the problems that we've  noticed over the past month which is  actually quite impressive since it could  be a lot worse and keep in mind that a  lot of these have to do with software so  they can get fixed with updates and  they'll get fixed over time when we get  better apple silicon support which is  very reassuring but if you've been  noticing any of those issues for  yourself go ahead and comment your  thoughts down below and be sure to click  the circle above to subscribe for more  videos like this one thanks for watching  and we'll see you in the next video  [Music]

